  <section class="why-choose-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The Three Highest Mountains in the UK</h2>
      <div class="why-choose-content">
        <p>
          If you only remember one fact from this UK hills map, make it this one: the three highest mountains in the UK are all in Scotland, and none of them are close to each other in height.
        </p>
        <table class="rankings-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Rank</th><th>Mountain</th><th>Range</th><th>Height</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1</td><td><a href="/mountain/ben-nevis/">Ben Nevis</a></td><td>Grampian Mountains</td><td>1,345m</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td><a href="/mountain/ben-macdui/">Ben Macdui</a></td><td>Cairngorms</td><td>1,309m</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3</td><td><a href="/mountain/braeriach/">Braeriach</a></td><td>Cairngorms</td><td>1,296m</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p><small>Source: Ordnance Survey</small></p>
        <p>
          Ben Nevis is 36m taller than Ben Macdui and holds the title outright as the highest point in the British Isles — not just Scotland.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-buttons">
          <a href="/mountains/" class="btn btn-primary">View All Mountains</a>
          <a href="/about/" class="btn btn-secondary">Learn More About Us</a>
